  "limitations": [
    "Pinned reference sizes are 64 B .. 2 MiB (16 sizes size[i]=1<<(i+6)), not 64 B .. 32 GB. Larger sizes are reachable through --sizes/--max-bytes.",
    "The reference has no device-to-device mode; D2D is validated against the host pattern only and has no runtime ratio.",
    "The OpenMP reference is an OpenMP target-offload program (icpx). Built with g++ -fopenmp it falls back to the host and moves no data, so it is not a CPU performance baseline; CPU correctness uses the byte-exact host reference."
  ]
